1
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:06,920
I'll marry into your family.

2
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:08,600
As for you,

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:10,320
you have to be my bottom, though.

4
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:11,720
This is actually nice.

5
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:12,240
P'Ing.

6
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:14,280
When something good happens to you,

7
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:15,880
it's natural to look radiant.

8
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:17,560
It's about that tryout at the boxing gym.

9
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:18,840
They want to sign me to a contract

10
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:20,440
and have me train in America.

11
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,360
But there's some good news.

12
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:23,680
I know him better than anyone.

13
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:24,640
My brother...

14
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:26,040
hates nothing more than being lied to.

15
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,160
The second you helped me,

16
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:29,120
you'd already betrayed him.

17
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:29,840
Itt...

18
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:32,800
Are we still friends?

19
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:44,840
My dear Fon, every single one of these...

20
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:46,320
is a hard pass.

21
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:49,400
I've already sent you a hundred designs, Mr. Ing.

22
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,600
These are the absolute bestsellers.

23
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,720
Bestsellers? So you mean

24
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,200
everyone and their mother has one?

25
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:56,080
No, that means

26
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:57,040
their designs are beautiful,

27
00:00:57,080 --> 00:00:59,160
so people buy them in droves.

28
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,040
Anyway, since these will be your couple rings,

29
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:02,280
why don't you let your partner

30
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:03,400
help you choose?

31
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:04,800
Oh, better not.

32
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,880
He has absolutely atrocious taste.

33
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:09,000
It's a struggle just to get him to dress decently.

34
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:11,360
Oh, atrocious taste?

35
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:12,480
Even with such terrible taste,

36
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:14,680
you're still into him?

37
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:16,400
Wow, that's quite interesting.

38
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:20,800
You talk too much. Are you doing this or not?

39
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:22,680
If not, I'll find another shop.

40
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:23,680
I can do it,

41
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:24,840
but a custom design

42
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:26,200
is gonna be very expensive.

43
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,200
Are you sure you can afford it?

44
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:29,120
Money isn't an issue.

45
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:30,720
Never mind, I'll design them myself.

46
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,160
Wait, but...

47
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:55,320
Mr. Ing, here's your coffee.

48
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,120
Should I clear away this trash?

49
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,560
Yeah, throw it all away.

50
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,960
Mr. Ing... Sir...

51
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:27,480
Yes?

52
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,960
Our investigation found that...

53
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:31,240
there's a firm called Private Equity

54
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:33,440
that gave 80 million to Green Agriculture.

55
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:35,120
-What? -That's likely the reason

56
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:36,680
they backed out of our deal.

57
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,400
It must be because of this payout.

58
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:41,120
I knew it.

59
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:44,680
That lowlife couple.

60
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:53,480
Hello, P'Ing?

61
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:54,720
Is something up?

62
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:55,320
Itt,

63
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:57,560
someone pumped 80 million into that couple.

64
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:59,240
What? I had no idea.

65
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:00,960
They're not even picking up my calls.

66
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,840
Every time I ask you something, you know nothing.

67
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:04,240
You're completely useless.

68
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:06,320
I'm sorry, P'Ing.

69
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:08,240
Save it. I don't want to hear your apologies.

70
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,360
Hold on.

71
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:11,480
We have dinner at home this Friday.

72
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:12,920
Don't forget to come.

73
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:16,079
Yeah.

74
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:35,280
Regarding Green Agriculture,

75
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:36,800
what should we do, Mr. Ing?

76
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:38,960
I'm not letting this slide.

77
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:39,960
Please help Itt

78
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,040
contact that couple

79
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,240
and get them in here to talk to me.

80
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,040
Yes, sir.

81
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:45,920
[Director Chatuphon]

82
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:53,720
Director, any updates on what's going on?

83
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:54,720
Yes.

84
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:57,040
That company submitted their documents today.

85
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:59,080
The content is exactly the same,

86
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:01,120
but they've changed the name of the shareholder

87
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:03,160
from your company to another one.

88
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:05,320
And do you happen to know

89
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:07,440
which company it is?

90
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:09,560
I'm looking into it.

91
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:11,560
I'll let you know as soon as I find out.

92
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:13,840
Director,

93
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,840
is it possible

94
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:19,200
for you to stall the approval?

95
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:21,840
If there's anything you need, just let me know.

96
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,000
I'll see what I can do, Mr. Ing.

97
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:25,000
Okay.

98
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:26,360
Thank you very much.

99
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,080
I'll be sure to return the favor.

100
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:33,280
Dammit.

101
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:35,360
We've been played for fools.

102
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:36,960
What happened?

103
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:39,480
That couple secretly switched the shareholder's name.

104
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:41,240
They submitted the documents

105
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,880
listing a different company.

106
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:50,800
Take a look for yourself.

107
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:02,440
"Pitak Real Estate Development Co., Ltd."

108
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:06,160
Registered capital is only fifty thousand baht.

109
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:09,800
The director's name is Mr. Thanapong.

110
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,560
With this little info, it's definitely a nominee.

111
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:13,880
Go check it out.

112
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,040
If the data is identical to ours,

113
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:16,760
it means it's an inside job.

114
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:17,880
As for this Mr. Pong,

115
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:19,480
find out exactly who he is.

116
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:20,840
Understood.

117
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,560
Do you not know, or are you hiding something from me?

118
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,760
For Yok's sake,

119
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:47,120
I'll get to the bottom of it first.

120
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:08,360
Come in.

121
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:18,720
Whoa.

122
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,320
Thought you said you were coming the day after tomorrow?

123
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:24,400
Hey.

124
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:26,280
I'm working.

125
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,520
Stop smoking already.

126
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:39,400
I was just worried that someone around here

127
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,120
would be so busy working he'd forget to eat,

128
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,400
so I made him this.

129
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:45,720
I'm just finding out

130
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:47,720
how great it is to date someone younger.

131
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:54,760
Shrimp, too.

132
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,440
How did you know I wanted shrimp?

133
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:00,640
Isn't it your favorite?

134
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:05,760
P'Ing,

135
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:08,360
wanna head home together after you finish eating?

136
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,040
Yok,

137
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:12,320
to be honest, I'm exhausted.

138
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,400
I still haven't finished my work.

139
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:15,200
The Pattaya project is giving me a massive headache.

140
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:20,200
Oh?

141
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:21,920
Are you mad?

142
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:24,800
Tell you what.

143
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,040
Once I'm done with work,

144
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:27,160
how about we go for a swim

145
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,960
in our new pool?

146
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,680
That's more like it.

147
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:35,840
Now, eat up.

148
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:39,480
Should I stop eating now?

149
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:41,960
No.

150
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:42,800
I'll eat the shrimp.

151
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,680
If I don't want this shrimp,

152
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,840
can I have some tiny shrimp instead?

153
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,800
Thanapong is a local.

154
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,400
Someone paid him a hundred thousand in cash

155
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:05,120
to register the company,

156
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:06,400
and he agreed to do it.

157
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:09,920
Okay. Thank you.

158
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:20,920
P'Ing,

159
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,640
is something wrong?

160
00:10:24,280 --> 00:10:26,400
Oh, it's nothing.

161
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:44,520
Honestly, I feel really bad for you.

162
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:46,960
I thought this project should've been

163
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,320
a perfect wrap-up before you left for America.

164
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:53,200
But in the end, it's just been a total mess.

165
00:10:55,680 --> 00:10:57,000
Let's stop talking about work.

166
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:01,960
Are you a strong swimmer?

167
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,160
Why?

168
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,880
I'm going to ride on your back.

169
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:09,840
Then how am I supposed to swim?

170
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:11,480
You don't have to swim. Just walk.

171
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:14,920
P'Ing...

172
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:15,640
What?

173
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:16,600
What kind of prank is this?

174
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,560
It's nothing.

175
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:23,880
Want to do it underwater?

176
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:25,240
Want to give it a try?

177
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:26,240
-No. -Come here.

178
00:11:26,280 --> 00:11:27,200
Come on.

179
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:28,160
Hold on.

180
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:30,520
P'Ing.

181
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:33,240
Are you trying to tease me?

182
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:35,640
Should we just do it underwater?

183
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,520
Let's go over there instead.

184
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:48,080
Dragon fruit today, huh?

185
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,280
Yes.

186
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:52,000
I really love dragon fruit.

187
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,600
Take the seeds out, too.

188
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:57,840
Are you messing with me?

189
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,880
I'm not. I'm serious.

190
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:01,520
Can you wait, then?

191
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:03,840
I could wait an eternity.

192
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,720
Your phone has been ringing nonstop.

193
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:09,400
Should you answer it?

194
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,680
Who is it?

195
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:14,440
How could they ruin my day?

196
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:16,280
I'll give them a piece of my mind.

197
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:20,200
You should answer it.

198
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:21,840
Okay.

199
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:24,280
Let's see

200
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:27,320
who's trying to ruin the mood.

201
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:31,160
Oh...

202
00:12:32,280 --> 00:12:33,360
It's Pite.

203
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:43,600
The number you have dialed is not in service.

204
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:46,080
Please check the number and try again.

205
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:54,720
Auntie,

206
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:56,200
has Pite already left?

207
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:57,280
He has.

208
00:12:57,520 --> 00:12:58,840
He just left today.

209
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:00,200
I know...

210
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:02,560
you did this for his own good,

211
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,960
but as his mother,

212
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:07,400
it's just so painful.

213
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:11,240
Auntie, to be honest with you,

214
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:13,160
I'm upset about it, too,

215
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:14,960
but it's for his own sake.

216
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:16,680
Once he gets out of there,

217
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:18,560
he'll definitely be more of a grown man.

218
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,000
Yeah.

219
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:22,400
I actually miss him, too.

220
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:25,120
Yes. Please don't worry.

221
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:29,800
Good riddance, you little jerk.

222
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:30,840
Dammit.

223
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:32,680
You know what?

224
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,840
I've been giving him money since he was a kid.

225
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:35,680
If it weren't for me,

226
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,840
he would've gotten beaten up so many times.

227
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:40,280
But then he had the nerve to double-cross me.

228
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:42,240
Can you believe how shameless he is?

229
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:47,760
Oh, hold on a second.

230
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:54,920
Look at this.

231
00:13:58,200 --> 00:13:59,840
Even though the Pattaya project hit a snag,

232
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:01,080
I have a new project to show you.

233
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,120
Here, it's a massive one.

234
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,720
The land in the north of Phuket?

235
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:10,960
This is the exact same set of data

236
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:12,720
that Itt sent me last time.

237
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:14,000
Wow.

238
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,080
What a memory. You're so smart.

239
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:23,040
The location is good.

240
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:24,560
How much of an investment is required?

241
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:28,360
Take a guess.

242
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,440
I wouldn't know.

243
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:40,760
Ten billion.

244
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,840
Ten billion?

245
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:46,640
Where are you gonna get that much money?

246
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:48,240
I've checked.

247
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:50,320
The company's current cash flow

248
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:52,520
is over a billion.

249
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:54,120
The only thing left is

250
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:55,760
to put our projects up as collateral.

251
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:57,160
I've already spoken to the bank.

252
00:14:58,080 --> 00:15:00,160
I'll mortgage the projects in Damnoen Saduak

253
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:01,440
and Samui.

254
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:03,840
That'll cover the full amount.

255
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:07,360
Have you checked everything thoroughly?

256
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:09,120
I've checked every detail.

257
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:11,120
I even sent a team to the site twice,

258
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:13,800
and they said the location is prime.

259
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,280
I don't support this.

260
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:21,200
It's way too risky.

261
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:23,680
What?

262
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:28,440
Since when did my Yok become such a cautious guy?

263
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:30,600
Now, listen.

264
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,440
Business...

265
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:34,240
is different from politics, you know?

266
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:36,880
It's about high risk, high return.

267
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:37,800
You can't just play it safe,

268
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:39,240
or you won't get rich.

269
00:15:40,520 --> 00:15:42,520
What about the funds for your other projects?

270
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:44,120
If even one thing goes wrong,

271
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,600
it'll trigger a chain reaction.

272
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:47,920
Why so fierce?

273
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,280
Don't overthink it.

274
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:51,440
I'm just pitching an idea.

275
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:52,800
What's there to be afraid of?

276
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:54,720
My brother...

277
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:56,640
hates nothing more than being lied to.

278
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,800
The second you helped me,

279
00:16:01,640 --> 00:16:02,840
you'd already betrayed him.

280
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:05,000
Then promise me

281
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:08,520
you'll always do your research before taking any risks.

282
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:14,280
What's with you today?

283
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:16,520
You sound like a nagging old man.

284
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:19,400
I'm just worried about you.

285
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:21,960
Worried?

286
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,480
Why would you be worried?

287
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:28,040
I'm just worried that once I'm abroad,

288
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:29,920
there won't be anyone to keep you in check.

289
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:36,400
So you're actually hooked on me.

290
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:38,200
Oh, right.

291
00:16:38,680 --> 00:16:40,480
You're going to America next week.

292
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:43,400
I'm sorry.

293
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,040
I've been so wrapped up in work I lost track of time.

294
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:48,960
I promise I'll be extra good in bed from now on.

295
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:53,440
Don't be sorry.

296
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:55,960
It's not your fault.

297
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:57,920
Here.

298
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:04,280
As for mine...

299
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,560
take the seeds out, too.

300
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:32,000
[Director Phadung]

301
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:36,760
Hello. You've got the information, right?

302
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:38,120
Yes.

303
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,520
Regarding that plot of land in Phuket,

304
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:43,440
the person who contacted the government is...

305
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:45,000
Mr. Itt.

306
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:47,880
Previously, he also submitted

307
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:50,520
the bilateral report himself.

308
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:52,520
Thank you very much, Director.

309
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:12,920
Itt...

310
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:16,960
I need to have a word with you.

311
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:19,320
Sure. What is it?

312
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:24,160
Mr. Ing, could you please sign these two documents?

313
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:25,440
What are you smiling about?

314
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:30,520
Mr. Yok has been gone for days.

315
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:33,000
He's back today, and his outfit is....

316
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:34,720
so cute.

317
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:39,800
He's here?

318
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:40,680
Yes.

319
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:42,320
I just walked past him a moment ago.

320
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:44,960
It looks like he's headed to a meeting with Mr. Itt

321
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:46,320
or someone.

322
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:50,280
What do those two need to meet about?

323
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:51,560
I'm not sure.

324
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:53,280
Would you like me to ask them?

325
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:54,440
Oh, no need.

326
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:56,520
I'll ask them myself.

327
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,600
You've checked my laptop,

328
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:08,400
even my entire chat history.

329
00:19:09,800 --> 00:19:11,600
Can you trust me now?

330
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:13,200
I wasn't using the Phuket project

331
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:14,440
to set a trap for anyone.

332
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,080
I already told you.

333
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:20,840
All I wanted was to get my cut from the Pattaya project.

334
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:24,040
I only helped a colleague write that report.

335
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:29,800
I'm sorry for doubting you.

336
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:44,040
We've been friends for so many years.

337
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,560
Don't you trust me at all?

338
00:19:53,200 --> 00:19:53,960
Itt,

339
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:55,640
I'm so sorry.

340
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:58,200
I let my emotions get the better of me.

341
00:19:59,480 --> 00:20:01,080
I didn't have any other motives.

342
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:02,200
You know,

343
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,520
you weren't like this.

344
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:19,800
Where are they?

345
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:23,360
I just don't understand.

346
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:25,560
You told me

347
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:27,240
that there was no way you'd ever be into guys.

348
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:32,120
It's not like that, Itt.

349
00:20:46,080 --> 00:20:47,480
Let me ask you something.

350
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:53,200
Do you actually like my brother?

351
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:57,680
When you realized you were into guys...

352
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:04,680
did you actually have a crush on me?

353
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:16,320
Yeah.

354
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:18,440
I really wanted to tell you how I felt.

355
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:20,480
Itt, you...

356
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,480
How dare you.

357
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:23,320
P'Ing.

358
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,200
Hey, P'Ing.

359
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:26,440
P'Ing, hey.

360
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:27,160
Hey.

361
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:28,720
Calm down, P'Ing.

362
00:21:28,760 --> 00:21:30,680
Calm down? Are you kidding me?

363
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:32,520
Calm down?

364
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:34,480
You think I'm an idiot?

365
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:36,600
You think you can just play me for a fool?

366
00:21:38,120 --> 00:21:39,000
And you, Itt.

367
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,640
You have the nerve to steal from me?

368
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:42,240
I asked you a question.

369
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:43,920
-How dare you. -P'Ing...

370
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:44,720
P'Ing...

371
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:45,480
Please.

372
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:47,480
What's your problem?

373
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:49,360
I see.

374
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:52,200
You were playing hard to get

375
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,320
because of this jerk, huh?

376
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:55,920
You've got eyes, but you're as blind as a bat.

377
00:21:56,160 --> 00:21:57,480
You might as well donate them.

378
00:21:58,760 --> 00:21:59,440
P'Ing...

379
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:00,760
Please let me explain first.

380
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:01,880
Explain what?

381
00:22:02,840 --> 00:22:04,200
Listen to me, both of you.

382
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:06,320
Don't let me see your faces here again.

383
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:08,880
Dammit.

384
00:22:11,040 --> 00:22:11,600
Hey.

385
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:12,880
He's furious right now.

386
00:22:12,920 --> 00:22:14,120
There's no use saying anything.

387
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:15,160
Leave me alone.

388
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:16,160
I need to talk to him.

389
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:25,320
P'Ing... Hey.

390
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:34,440
♪ Now it's breaking me apart ♪

391
00:22:35,360 --> 00:22:42,160
♪ It's my fault for every broken part we had ♪

392
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:49,240
♪ We had a warm run, babe ♪

393
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:52,960
♪ I messed up all that we were ♪

394
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:55,840
[20 missed calls from Yok]

395
00:22:57,880 --> 00:22:58,680
Dammit.

396
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:04,160
♪ Our sweetest spark turned to the dark ♪

397
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:05,160
Damn...

398
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:09,160
♪ Turned to the dark ♪

399
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:14,200
♪ I know what I have done wrong ♪

400
00:23:15,040 --> 00:23:16,040
Itt...

401
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:22,320
You know that we can't go public,

402
00:23:22,320 --> 00:23:23,520
but you did that today

403
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:26,560
while P'Phet and Itt were right there.

404
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:34,840
What's this?

405
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:37,760
If I gave you a ring, would you take it?

406
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:43,000
That sentence you didn't get to finish...

407
00:23:44,280 --> 00:23:45,640
You'd say you liked me, right?

408
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:47,080
Yeah.

409
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:48,640
Dammit.

410
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:51,440
Just go to hell, Yok.

411
00:24:11,800 --> 00:24:12,680
This little jerk...

412
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:17,240
Who let you into my house?

413
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:21,200
We need to talk, P'Ing.

414
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:22,920
Talk about what? Go talk to Itt.

415
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:23,920
I don't want to talk to you.

416
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:25,920
I only want to see you.

417
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:27,360
But I don't want to see you.

418
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:30,160
Can you just calm down?

419
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:31,440
Stop yelling at me.

420
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:34,160
Fine, talk.

421
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:38,440
Stay away from me.

422
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:43,360
Just listen to me.

423
00:24:47,160 --> 00:24:48,280
I admit it.

424
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:51,360
I really couldn't understand my feelings.

425
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:54,800
I felt like I wanted to protect Itt when we were younger.

426
00:24:57,680 --> 00:24:59,000
Protect him from what?

427
00:25:01,640 --> 00:25:02,920
Please listen to me.

428
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:07,920
When I first met him,

429
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:11,600
he told me you'd always bullied him.

430
00:25:15,800 --> 00:25:17,160
Help me.

431
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:21,440
P'Ing, please pull me up.

432
00:25:28,560 --> 00:25:30,080
What? That situation?

433
00:25:31,040 --> 00:25:32,240
Are you out of your mind?

434
00:25:33,760 --> 00:25:35,440
I was actually teaching him how to swim.

435
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:36,560
He didn't know how to swim.

436
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:38,680
Then his mom saw us and made a huge scene,

437
00:25:38,680 --> 00:25:40,000
so I never got to finish teaching him.

438
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:41,320
Now listen to me.

439
00:25:41,440 --> 00:25:42,560
If I really wanted to kill him,

440
00:25:42,560 --> 00:25:44,040
I would have just kicked him into the pool.

441
00:25:47,480 --> 00:25:49,520
I'm right here. You're not going to die.

442
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:52,040
Please pull me up.

443
00:25:52,520 --> 00:25:53,640
P'Ing, please.

444
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:55,200
Don't be such a wimp.

445
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:56,440
The water only reaches your chest.

446
00:25:57,040 --> 00:25:58,160
Now, stand up.

447
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:00,720
P'Ing, help me.

448
00:26:01,680 --> 00:26:02,480
Itt.

449
00:26:02,520 --> 00:26:03,960
Let go of my son right now.

450
00:26:09,320 --> 00:26:11,640
Don't let him teach you anything now.

451
00:26:14,280 --> 00:26:15,160
[Swimming Manual for Children]

452
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:16,720
Yok,

453
00:26:17,360 --> 00:26:18,760
is the Ing you know

454
00:26:19,320 --> 00:26:20,800
really that stupid?

455
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:21,800
Is he?

456
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:24,760
I admit...

457
00:26:24,840 --> 00:26:26,280
that I act like a tyrant

458
00:26:26,320 --> 00:26:27,280
and have a nasty temper,

459
00:26:27,320 --> 00:26:28,960
but I've never tried to hurt anyone.

460
00:26:32,520 --> 00:26:33,720
Okay, maybe a little bit.

461
00:26:34,520 --> 00:26:35,720
But if I wanted to be cruel,

462
00:26:35,960 --> 00:26:37,840
he and his mom wouldn't be living in my house.

463
00:26:40,600 --> 00:26:42,240
I didn't know you back then.

464
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:44,920
I only knew one side of the story.

465
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:49,800
I heard what Itt's mom said, and...

466
00:26:50,280 --> 00:26:51,280
when I met you,

467
00:26:51,680 --> 00:26:53,280
you were always on a power trip with him.

468
00:26:53,360 --> 00:26:55,320
I only act that way because of his mom.

469
00:26:55,360 --> 00:26:56,720
It's got nothing to do with him.

470
00:26:56,960 --> 00:26:58,920
I've always seen him as my brother.

471
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:01,160
Otherwise, why would I let him intern at my company?

472
00:27:01,720 --> 00:27:02,360
Why?

473
00:27:02,400 --> 00:27:04,200
Why would I have let him take on major projects?

474
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:05,680
I wouldn't have given him those opportunities.

475
00:27:13,280 --> 00:27:14,080
Ing...

476
00:27:16,120 --> 00:27:17,240
From now on,

477
00:27:18,400 --> 00:27:20,440
you must take good care of your younger brother.

478
00:27:31,920 --> 00:27:33,080
I'm entrusting him to you.

479
00:27:38,320 --> 00:27:39,200
Give it back.

480
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:40,640
Hey, give it back.

481
00:27:40,680 --> 00:27:41,760
Give it back to me.

482
00:27:42,280 --> 00:27:43,280
Give it to me.

483
00:27:45,040 --> 00:27:47,440
He's my brother. Only I can mess with him.

484
00:27:48,160 --> 00:27:49,160
You want some more?

485
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:51,320
Huh? You want more?

486
00:27:52,800 --> 00:27:53,680
Do you?

487
00:27:57,320 --> 00:27:58,720
Yeah, I admit it.

488
00:27:59,800 --> 00:28:01,640
My patience with him is paper-thin.

489
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:02,720
Just look at him.

490
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:04,240
He's such a crybaby.

491
00:28:04,240 --> 00:28:05,800
It's only natural that I'd be annoyed.

492
00:28:06,240 --> 00:28:07,440
Listen to me.

493
00:28:07,480 --> 00:28:09,080
Given what his mom did to me,

494
00:28:09,120 --> 00:28:10,520
you could say I went pretty easy on him.

495
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:15,960
I get it now.

496
00:28:18,760 --> 00:28:20,440
You may act tough, but you're actually kind.

497
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:22,960
It's my fault

498
00:28:23,800 --> 00:28:25,880
for believing only what Itt told me.

499
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:31,120
Finally.

500
00:28:36,160 --> 00:28:38,040
We've cleared the air now, right?

501
00:28:39,440 --> 00:28:41,240
I'm leaving in two days.

502
00:28:42,160 --> 00:28:44,280
I don't want us to have any more misunderstandings.

503
00:28:45,760 --> 00:28:46,560
Yeah, I know.

504
00:28:49,800 --> 00:28:50,680
P'Ing.

505
00:28:51,640 --> 00:28:52,920
Please forgive me.

506
00:28:54,320 --> 00:28:55,760
How can I make it up to you?

507
00:29:03,600 --> 00:29:04,520
It's simple.

508
00:29:06,280 --> 00:29:07,680
Just be on the bottom

509
00:29:07,680 --> 00:29:09,120
and let me top you.

510
00:29:12,320 --> 00:29:14,440
I figured you'd say that.

511
00:29:16,760 --> 00:29:17,840
Then...

512
00:29:18,360 --> 00:29:19,840
how about we save it for your birthday?

513
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:23,440
You can fly out to see me,

514
00:29:23,640 --> 00:29:24,720
or...

515
00:29:24,960 --> 00:29:26,480
I can fly back here to see you.

516
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:29,600
I'll let you have your way then.

517
00:29:30,520 --> 00:29:32,160
But...

518
00:29:32,960 --> 00:29:33,800
as for right now...

519
00:29:33,840 --> 00:29:34,560
What?

520
00:29:35,320 --> 00:29:37,600
Hey. Hey...

521
00:29:38,080 --> 00:29:40,680
No, I want it today. Stop now.

522
00:29:57,320 --> 00:29:58,520
P'Ing.

523
00:29:58,520 --> 00:30:00,720
P'Ing, help me.

524
00:30:00,760 --> 00:30:01,960
P'Ing.

525
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:03,920
P'Ing...

526
00:30:04,160 --> 00:30:05,320
What's up, you little jerk?

527
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:06,560
P'Ing...

528
00:30:06,600 --> 00:30:09,240
Please help me. I'm so sorry.

529
00:30:10,760 --> 00:30:12,080
Please let me come home.

530
00:30:12,360 --> 00:30:13,560
If you keep me here any longer,

531
00:30:13,560 --> 00:30:15,560
I'm going to lose my mind.

532
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:16,880
Shut up, Pite.

533
00:30:17,040 --> 00:30:18,440
Stop your damn screaming.

534
00:30:19,400 --> 00:30:21,120
If you want to come back, listen to me.

535
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:22,440
Just give me my condo units back

536
00:30:22,480 --> 00:30:24,320
or pay me back every single cent.

537
00:30:24,320 --> 00:30:25,720
Come on, P'Ing...

538
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:28,320
How am I supposed to get that kind of money?

539
00:30:29,040 --> 00:30:29,800
I'm begging you.

540
00:30:29,800 --> 00:30:31,920
This place is a total wasteland.

541
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:32,960
There's no signal.

542
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:34,280
There aren't even any girls.

543
00:30:34,320 --> 00:30:35,920
I have to wake up at five every morning,

544
00:30:36,080 --> 00:30:37,800
and I'm getting hazed left and right.

545
00:30:37,800 --> 00:30:41,280
Please let me come back. I'm begging you.

546
00:30:41,800 --> 00:30:43,480
Listen to me, Pite.

547
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:45,000
All these years,

548
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:46,440
when have I ever wronged you?

549
00:30:46,560 --> 00:30:48,760
I've always taken care of you and given you money.

550
00:30:48,800 --> 00:30:51,240
But you chose to repay me by ripping me off.

551
00:30:54,880 --> 00:30:55,720
P'Ing...

552
00:30:55,760 --> 00:30:57,520
I'm really sorry.

553
00:30:57,560 --> 00:30:59,280
I didn't mean to do it.

554
00:30:59,800 --> 00:31:01,400
I was in so much debt.

555
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:03,080
They had a gun pointed at my neck.

556
00:31:03,080 --> 00:31:05,440
Was I just supposed to let them kill me?

557
00:31:06,480 --> 00:31:07,560
Besides,

558
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:09,320
Itt told me to do it.

559
00:31:09,360 --> 00:31:11,400
I wouldn't have the guts to do it on my own.

560
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:13,080
Wait, Pite.

561
00:31:13,480 --> 00:31:14,680
What did you just say?

562
00:31:15,200 --> 00:31:16,480
P'Ing...

563
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:18,920
The reason I've been avoiding you

564
00:31:19,080 --> 00:31:21,000
isn't because I was afraid you'd beat me up.

565
00:31:21,720 --> 00:31:23,600
Well, I was afraid of that, too.

566
00:31:23,600 --> 00:31:25,120
Pite, start talking.

567
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:26,480
What does Itt have to do with this?

568
00:31:26,520 --> 00:31:27,080
Tell me

569
00:31:27,080 --> 00:31:27,840
what he has to do with this.

570
00:31:27,840 --> 00:31:30,720
Please help me. I'm scared.

571
00:31:41,320 --> 00:31:43,480
P'Ing, you should cut back on smoking.

572
00:31:43,520 --> 00:31:44,440
Get over here.

573
00:31:50,800 --> 00:31:52,400
Pite called me today.

574
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:55,360
Care to guess...

575
00:31:56,160 --> 00:31:57,320
what he had to say?

576
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:01,280
I assume he was begging you

577
00:32:01,280 --> 00:32:03,000
to let him come home.

578
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:06,120
Exactly.

579
00:32:17,880 --> 00:32:19,400
He also told me...

580
00:32:20,840 --> 00:32:23,440
that those three condo units I intended for Mr. Pha-nu

581
00:32:25,240 --> 00:32:26,560
have been pocketed by you.

582
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:41,800
You wanna die that badly?

583
00:32:43,400 --> 00:32:44,200
Guess what?

584
00:32:44,920 --> 00:32:46,840
My plan was full of holes,

585
00:32:48,040 --> 00:32:49,720
but you didn't suspect me at all.

586
00:32:51,120 --> 00:32:52,520
Since you trusted me so much,

587
00:32:53,400 --> 00:32:54,680
I'm genuinely touched.

588
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:56,240
You little punk.

589
00:32:57,880 --> 00:32:58,680
What?

590
00:32:59,720 --> 00:33:01,960
This is the birthday gift you gave me.

591
00:33:09,320 --> 00:33:10,760
I'm not that same little brother

592
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:13,440
you can bully whenever you feel like it anymore.

593
00:33:18,360 --> 00:33:19,440
Ing, Itt.

594
00:33:19,640 --> 00:33:20,720
Open the door right now.

595
00:33:20,720 --> 00:33:21,920
Stop fighting.

596
00:33:22,240 --> 00:33:23,320
-Itt. -Open the door.

597
00:33:23,360 --> 00:33:24,480
-Ing. -Open the door.

598
00:33:24,680 --> 00:33:25,720
Ing, Itt.

599
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:26,880
Stop fighting this instant.

600
00:33:26,920 --> 00:33:28,960
I love the look on your face right now.

601
00:33:30,640 --> 00:33:31,920
It's like...

602
00:33:33,560 --> 00:33:34,840
in your eyes,

603
00:33:35,760 --> 00:33:37,440
everyone is just trash.

604
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:41,640
What a waste...

605
00:33:42,920 --> 00:33:44,640
I actually thought about being nice to you.

606
00:33:45,680 --> 00:33:46,680
Being nice to me?

607
00:33:47,720 --> 00:33:48,520
Why?

608
00:33:49,040 --> 00:33:50,360
Because of a jerk like Yok?

609
00:33:52,360 --> 00:33:53,960
Stay the hell out of this.

610
00:33:57,480 --> 00:33:59,800
I love it when you're so mad you're literally shaking

611
00:34:00,640 --> 00:34:02,000
but can't do a thing about it.

612
00:34:06,760 --> 00:34:08,719
Since we were kids, you've always acted so superior

613
00:34:08,760 --> 00:34:10,040
and looked down on me.

614
00:34:11,040 --> 00:34:12,120
I kept dreaming

615
00:34:12,679 --> 00:34:14,199
about what it would be like

616
00:34:14,920 --> 00:34:16,040
to have the upper hand over you.

617
00:34:19,639 --> 00:34:20,440
Damn you.

618
00:34:25,320 --> 00:34:26,639
Hey, Ing.

619
00:34:27,960 --> 00:34:29,120
You're hitting your brother again.

620
00:34:29,600 --> 00:34:30,920
You're an adult now.

621
00:34:31,360 --> 00:34:32,600
Why do you keep doing this to him?

622
00:34:32,639 --> 00:34:34,800
Because this jerk did some messed-up things to me.

623
00:34:35,120 --> 00:34:36,560
Stop taking his side already.

624
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:38,040
By the way,

625
00:34:39,520 --> 00:34:40,840
you should know...

626
00:34:41,600 --> 00:34:44,040
that this isn't entirely my fault.

627
00:34:45,560 --> 00:34:46,600
As for the rest,

628
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:49,320
why don't you ask Yok?

629
00:35:16,880 --> 00:35:17,640
Hello?

630
00:35:17,640 --> 00:35:18,680
Mr. Ing,

631
00:35:18,720 --> 00:35:20,560
the investigation is complete.

632
00:35:21,080 --> 00:35:23,360
This file contains Mr. Itt's financial records.

633
00:35:24,240 --> 00:35:25,520
From these records,

634
00:35:25,640 --> 00:35:28,560
I also managed to track down Private Equity

635
00:35:28,680 --> 00:35:31,480
that's behind Green Agriculture.

636
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:32,880
Mr. Ing,

637
00:35:33,120 --> 00:35:34,600
please prepare yourself before opening it.

638
00:35:34,640 --> 00:35:36,080
There are two shareholders.

639
00:35:50,880 --> 00:35:56,880
[Major Shareholders Prutta, Tottiwa]

640
00:36:45,920 --> 00:36:47,120
Get a doctor in here.

641
00:36:47,120 --> 00:36:49,320
I don't care if they give me drugs or electric shocks.

642
00:36:49,360 --> 00:36:51,440
Just make it all stop so I can finally rest.

643
00:36:51,600 --> 00:36:52,840
What's going on between you and Mr. Ing?

644
00:36:52,840 --> 00:36:53,720
Have you met him yet?

645
00:36:53,760 --> 00:36:55,800
Instead of wasting your time on me,

646
00:36:55,800 --> 00:36:57,640
you should be helping your brother.

647
00:36:57,840 --> 00:36:59,200
What happened to P'Phet?

648
00:36:59,240 --> 00:37:01,160
Quit Araya Group right now.

649
00:37:01,360 --> 00:37:02,680
Thanks so much

650
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:04,920
for giving me all the love that wasn't even real.

651
00:37:05,560 --> 00:37:07,600
From now on,

652
00:37:07,880 --> 00:37:09,000
we're over.

653
00:37:09,040 --> 00:37:10,280
P'Ing, wait...

654
00:37:10,320 --> 00:37:12,560
-We can't end things like this. -Dammit.

655
00:37:12,560 --> 00:37:13,880
Once this is settled,

656
00:37:14,320 --> 00:37:15,760
I'll come back to you.
